# What the test suite needs, exact pins rather than `>=` floors.
# tests/requirements.txt is compiled from this file with hashes and installed
# with --require-hashes and wheels only, by the `Tests` job in
# .github/workflows/pull-request.yml and by `make coverage`.
# Regenerate it with the command in its header, never by hand; Renovate's
# pip-compile manager bumps a pin here and replays that command.
#
# A floor resolves to whatever is newest on PyPI when the job runs, which puts
# the seven day `minimumReleaseAge` in .github/renovate.json5 out of the loop:
# that window governs when Renovate proposes a change, not what pip installs.
# An exact pin is also the only shape the `requirement_line` grammar in
# .github/pin-only.yml recognizes, and the lock is graded by its
# `hash_locked_requirements` grammar, so a bump can take the unattended lane.
#
# pytest-cov is needed because pytest.ini's addopts passes --cov, and it
# writes the report SonarQube Cloud reads; coverage is what measures. pyyaml
# is imported by the suite and by src/pin_only.py.
coverage==7.16.2
pytest==9.1.1
pytest-cov==7.1.0
pyyaml==6.0.3
